Maya (Design): usability session notes: on small landscape the audit table and right rail clash. action menu gets pushed under the rail and becomes hard to reach. screenshot attached. :camera:
Theo (Frontend): thanks — can you share the exact emulator size?
Luca (QA): repro steps: Console > Audit > rotate to landscape on foldable emulator (viewport 528w, safe-area 24 each side). effective content width ~480. Right rail overlays table actions when window is narrow.
Rae (PM): product goals: keep primary audit actions reachable without horizontal scroll, preserve status badges, and avoid hiding primary nav.
Maya (Design): proposed pattern: at <=560 switch table -> stacked list. Move per-row actions into an "Actions" disclosure button; show primary status chip inline at top-left of the stacked card; keep right rail collapsible into a bottom sheet on narrow landscape.
Theo (Frontend): implementation idea: CSS-first stacked switch + tiny JS that moves the actions node into the disclosure to preserve event handlers. Example:
```
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .audit-table { display:block; }
  .audit-row { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; padding:12px; }
  .status-chip { order:-1; align-self:flex-start; min-height:44px; padding:8px 12px; }
}
```
Maya (Design): accessibility: ensure each stacked field has a visible label (e.g., "User: Alice") and that the disclosure button is labelled "Actions" with aria-expanded. Also ensure focus returns correctly after selecting an action.
Luca (QA): tests to add: rotate tests on Pixel Fold, hit-target verification (>=44px), SR readouts for stacked rows, and right-rail collapse/restore behavior. I'll file RF-5051.
Rae (PM): decision: implement stacked cards at <=560, move actions into a labelled "Actions" disclosure, convert right rail to collapsible bottom sheet on narrow landscape, and gate behind feature flag for staged rollout. Theo, estimate?
Theo (Frontend): ~2.5 dev-days + 1 QA day. I'll add a feature flag and unit tests for the DOM migration.
Maya (Design): uploading updated mock: https://assets.redwood.internal/designs/audit-stacked-actions-v1.png ; also adding copy suggestion: disclosure label should read "Actions" not "More".
design-bot: mock uploaded: https://assets.redwood.internal/designs/audit-stacked-actions-v1.png
Rae (PM): thanks all — Theo please raise PR to feature branch, Luca will validate, Maya will hand off final tokens and accessible labels. Closing until PR review. :white_check_mark:
